ell>58.5</cell><cell>62.6</cell><cell>23.0</cell><cell>n/a</cell><cell>4.8</cell></row><row><cell>Territory: Open</cell><cell>SC 0 SC 1</cell><cell>53.1 60.4</cell><cell>7.3 7.1</cell><cell>44.3 58.2</cell><cell>21.1 19.3</cell><cell>40.5 94.2</cell><cell>17.1 39.0</cell><cell>45.1 60.5</cell><cell>4.7 7.5</cell></row><row><cell></cell><cell>univ.</cell><cell>63.0</cell><cell>14.9</cell><cell>54.1</cell><cell>47.0</cell><cell>57.7</cell><cell>25.6</cell><cell>n/a</cell><cell>4.9</cell></row><row><cell></cell><cell>S-P</cell><cell>236.3</cell><cell>199.4</cell><cell>220.3</cell><cell>112.2</cell><cell>54.4</cell><cell>233.3</cell><cell>n/a</cell><cell>10.4</cell></row><row><cell>Territory: Rooms</cell><cell>SC 0 SC 1</cell><cell>186.4 27.3</cell><cell>160.4 12.9</cell><cell>158.0 6.2</cell><cell>70.6 15.3</cell><cell>128.0 5.7</cell><cell>161.5 4.3</cell><cell>203.8 273.4</cell><cell>9.1 1.8</cell></row><row><cell></cell><cell>univ.</cell><cell>230.2</cell><cell>189.8</cell><cell>192.6</cell><cell>134.6</cell><cell>56.0</cell><cell>220.6</cell><cell>n/a</cell><cell>10.2</cell></row></table></figure>\n\t\t\t<note xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" place=\"foot\" n=\"1\" xml:id=\"foot_0\"><p>The largest category of extant research that we left unrepresented is communication/language (e.g.<ref type=\"bibr\" target=\"#b36\">Lazaridou &amp; Baroni (2020)</ref>;<ref type=\"bibr\" target=\"#b45\">Lowe et al. (2019)</ref>;Mordatch &amp; Abbeel (2018)). We see no reason why scenarios engaging these ideas could not be added in the future. Turn-based games (e.g.<ref type=\"bibr\" target=\"#b35\">Lanctot et al. (2019)</ref>) and games involving physics (e.g.<ref type=\"bibr\" target=\"#b43\">Liu et al. (2018)</ref>) were also omitted.</p></note>\n\t\t\t<note xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" place=\"foot\" n=\"2\" xml:id=\"foot_1\"><p>For a video of Allelopathic Harvest, see https://youtu. be/ESugMMdKLxI.</p></note>\n\t\t\t<note xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" place=\"foot\" n=\"3\" xml:id=\"foot_2\"><p>For a video of Arena Running with Scissors in the Matrix, see https://youtu.be/esXPyGBIf2Y.</p></note>\n\t\t\t<note xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" place=\"foot\" n=\"4\" xml:id=\"foot_3\"><p>For a video of Bach or Stravinsky in the Matrix, see https: //youtu.be/SiFjSyCp2Ss.</p></note>\n\t\t\t<note xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" place=\"foot\" n=\"5\" xml:id=\"foot_4\"><p>For a video of Capture the Flag, see https://youtu.be/ VRNt55-0IqE.</p></note>\n\t\t\t<note xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" place=\"foot\" n=\"6\" xml:id=\"foot_5\"><p>For a video of Chemistry: Branched Chain Reaction, see https://youtu.be/ZhRB-_ruoH8.</p></note>\n\t\t\t<note xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" place=\"foot\" n=\"7\" xml:id=\"foot_6\"><p>For a video of Chemistry: Metabolic cycles, see https: //youtu.be/oFK9VujhpeI.</p></note>\n\t\t\t<note xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" place=\"foot\" n=\"8\" xml:id=\"foot_7\"><p>For a video of Chicken in the Matrix, see https://youtu. be/uhAb2busSDY.</p></note>\n\t\t\t<note xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" place=\"foot\" n=\"9\" xml:id=\"foot_8\"><p>For a video of Clean Up, see https://youtu.be/ jOeIunFtTS0.</p></note>\n\t\t\t<note xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" place=\"foot\" n=\"10\" xml:id=\"foot_9\"><p>For a video of Collaborative Cooking: Impassable, see https://youtu.be/yn1uSNymQ_U.</p></note>\n\t\t\t<note xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" place=\"foot\" n=\"11\" xml:id=\"foot_10\"><p>For a video of Collaborative Cooking: Passable, see https: //youtu.be/R_TBitc3hto.</p></note>\n\t\t\t<note xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" place=\"foot\" n=\"12\" xml:id=\"foot_11\"><p>For a video of Commons Harvest: Closed, see https:// youtu.be/ZHjrlTft98M.</p></note>\n\t\t\t<note xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" place=\"foot\" n=\"18\" xml:id=\"foot_12\"><p>For a video of Rationalizable Coordination in the Matrix, see https://youtu.be/BpHpoir06mY.</p></note>\n\t\t\t<note xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" place=\"foot\" n=\"19\" xml:id=\"foot_13\"><p>For a video of Running with Scissors in the Matrix, see https://youtu.be/oqYd4Ib5g70.</p></note>\n\t\t\t<note xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" place=\"foot\" n=\"20\" xml:id=\"foot_14\"><p>For a video of Stag Hunt in the Matrix, see https:// youtu.be/7fVHUH4siOQ.</p></note>\n\t\t\t<note xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" place=\"foot\" n=\"21\" xml:id=\"foot_15\"><p>For a video of Territory: Open, see https://youtu.be/ 3hB8lABa6nI.</p></note>\n\t\t\t<note xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" place=\"foot\" n=\"22\" xml:id=\"foot_16\"><p>For a video of Territory: Rooms, see https://youtu.be/ u0YOiShqzA4.</p></note>\n\t\t</body>\n\t\t<back>\n\n\t\t\t<div type=\"acknowledgement\">\n<div><p>Acknowledgements H. References A. Secondary evaluation metrics G. Acknowledgements The authors would like to thank: <rs type=\"person\">Richard Everett</rs>, <rs type=\"person\">DJ Strouse</rs>, <rs type=\"person\">Kevin McKee</rs>, and <rs type=\"person\">Edward Hughes</rs> for contributing to substrate development; <rs type=\"person\">Mary Cassin</rs> for contributing artwork; and <rs type=\"person\">Steven Wheelwright</rs> for help building an early version of the evaluation system.</p><p>H. References</p></div>\n\t\t\t</div>\t\t\t<div type=\"annex\">\n<div xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\"><p>Appendix Contents A. Secondary evaluation metrics B. Substrate details C. Agent architecture details D. Training setup E. Scenario details F. Raw performance scores G.</p></div>\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t<div type=\"references\">\n\n\t\t\t\t<listBibl>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b0\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">D</forename><surname>Amodei</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">C</forename><surname>Olah</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"firs